WEBVTT

00:00:06.614 --> 00:00:10.935
the secret of the stones by Victoria Hu.

00:00:10.995 --> 00:00:26.656
Chapter 1.

00:00:26.716 --> 00:00:41.927
Laura and Max are twins.

00:00:41.986 --> 00:00:45.649
They live in London with their mum and dad.

00:00:45.709 --> 00:00:49.582
They always have interesting adventures on holiday.

00:00:49.642 --> 00:00:53.654
They visit different cities and countries.

00:00:53.714 --> 00:00:59.457
This summer, they are going to stay in a small cottage in the country.

00:00:59.517 --> 00:01:05.426
The cottage is in a village called Stone Cross near Salisbury.

00:01:05.485 --> 00:01:10.524
Max and Laura aren't very happy.

00:01:10.584 --> 00:01:12.876
Boring.

00:01:12.935 --> 00:01:14.496
Says Max.

00:01:14.556 --> 00:01:16.738
He looks at the map.

00:01:16.798 --> 00:01:19.630
The cottage is in the middle of a field.

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:22.602
What can we do in the middle of a field?

00:01:22.662 --> 00:01:24.934
Why are we going there?

00:01:24.994 --> 00:01:26.796
asks Laura.

00:01:26.855 --> 00:01:29.938
Their dad is very tired.

00:01:29.997 --> 00:01:34.071
He says he wants to relax and to sleep a lot.

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:36.642
Their mum loves the country.

00:01:36.702 --> 00:01:39.285
She wants to walk and print.

00:01:39.344 --> 00:01:42.816
It's a very beautiful part of England, she says.

00:01:42.876 --> 00:01:46.969
Full of culture, tradition, mystery, mystery.

00:01:46.989 --> 00:01:49.200
Say Max and Laura together.

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:50.171
Mystery?

00:01:50.191 --> 00:01:56.384
Okay, let's go.

00:01:56.444 --> 00:02:08.191
Chapter Two, Stone Cross.

00:02:08.251 --> 00:02:17.725
The next day, Uncle Stephen and Auntie Barbara arrive.

00:02:17.785 --> 00:02:20.186
They have lots of suitcases.

00:02:20.246 --> 00:02:25.149
This year, the two families are going on holiday together.

00:02:25.209 --> 00:02:27.740
Mum drives her car.

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:29.341
Dad sleeps.

00:02:29.401 --> 00:02:31.592
Dad always sleeps.

00:02:31.652 --> 00:02:37.656
Uncle Stephen and Auntie Barbara follow in their slow old car.

00:02:37.716 --> 00:02:44.642
Two hours later, they arrive at Stone Cross and find their cottage in the middle of the field.

00:02:44.702 --> 00:02:52.266
There are green hills, beautiful cottages, flowers, sheep, and cows everywhere.

00:02:52.326 --> 00:02:54.198
It's lovely!

00:02:54.258 --> 00:02:55.949
Say Max and Laura.

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:58.010
It's perfect!

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:00.332
Say Mum and Auntie Barbara.

00:03:00.392 --> 00:03:02.374
Dad says nothing.

00:03:02.434 --> 00:03:05.184
He is sleeping in the car.

00:03:05.244 --> 00:03:07.615
What do you think, Stephen?

00:03:07.675 --> 00:03:09.315
Do you like it?

00:03:09.375 --> 00:03:12.026
Uncle Stephen doesn't answer.

00:03:12.086 --> 00:03:14.507
He is looking into the distance.

00:03:14.567 --> 00:03:18.868
His eyes are very black and strange.

00:03:18.928 --> 00:03:21.349
What's the matter, Stephen?

00:03:21.409 --> 00:03:23.150
Ask Santi Barbara.

00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:25.890
Don't you like the cottage?

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:28.352
Yes, it's wonderful.

00:03:28.412 --> 00:03:29.252
He says.

00:03:29.312 --> 00:03:30.442
Come on, everyone.

00:03:30.502 --> 00:03:33.078
Let's take these suitcases inside.

00:03:33.138 --> 00:03:34.754
Wake up, Andrew.

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:37.446
Dad wakes up.

00:03:37.506 --> 00:03:39.928
Where are we?

00:03:39.988 --> 00:03:41.680
We're here at Stone Cross.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:42.660
Come and help.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:45.353
We must take the suitcases into the cottage.

00:03:45.412 --> 00:03:48.705
They take the suitcases and go inside.

00:03:48.765 --> 00:03:51.276
But Uncle Stephen waits.

00:03:51.336 --> 00:03:53.839
He wants to talk to his wife.

00:03:53.899 --> 00:03:56.811
Barbara, I must tell you something.

00:03:56.871 --> 00:04:00.386
He says, his voice is very serious.

00:04:00.446 --> 00:04:01.849
This place?

00:04:01.909 --> 00:04:03.100
Yes, darling.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:05.482
This place is in my book.

00:04:05.542 --> 00:04:07.043
Do you remember?

00:04:07.103 --> 00:04:10.966
The book I am studying about mysteries.

00:04:11.026 --> 00:04:14.559
But Stephen, that book is very old.

00:04:14.619 --> 00:04:18.692
It's full of strange codes and secret messages.

00:04:18.752 --> 00:04:19.963
Exactly.

00:04:20.023 --> 00:04:21.574
Don't you understand?

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:23.706
This is the place where...

00:04:23.766 --> 00:04:25.966
Come on, Barbara.

00:04:26.026 --> 00:04:28.766
Shout's mum from the cottage.

00:04:28.826 --> 00:04:30.396
We're coming!

00:04:30.456 --> 00:04:33.428
Uncle Steven and Auntie Barbara answer.

00:04:33.488 --> 00:04:37.619
But when they walk to the cottage, their faces are white.

00:04:37.679 --> 00:04:43.892
They look very worried.

00:04:43.951 --> 00:04:49.384
Chapter three.

00:04:49.444 --> 00:04:56.734
Mr. Carter and Mrs. Black.

00:04:56.794 --> 00:05:02.715
The cottage is big.

00:05:02.774 --> 00:05:06.578
There are four bedrooms and two bathrooms upstairs.

00:05:06.638 --> 00:05:11.392
Downstairs, there is a big kitchen, a living room and a study.

00:05:11.452 --> 00:05:14.554
Uncle Stephen wants to use the study.

00:05:14.614 --> 00:05:17.928
He must finish some work during the holiday.

00:05:17.988 --> 00:05:21.250
Uncle Stephen is a historian.

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:24.052
What does Uncle Stephen do exactly?

00:05:24.112 --> 00:05:25.464
Laura asks.

00:05:25.524 --> 00:05:28.822
Her mother replies, He studies history.

00:05:28.882 --> 00:05:31.392
Max is confused.

00:05:31.452 --> 00:05:34.074
But I study history too.

00:05:34.134 --> 00:05:35.316
At school.

00:05:35.376 --> 00:05:36.787
But it's not my job.

00:05:36.847 --> 00:05:40.991
Yes, but Uncle Stephen writes books about history.

00:05:41.051 --> 00:05:43.484
He thinks about history.

00:05:43.544 --> 00:05:47.608
He tries to understand the things that no one understands.

00:05:47.668 --> 00:05:50.000
For example, asks Laura.

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:52.562
Well, mum replies.

00:05:52.621 --> 00:05:56.312
For example, the mystery of Stonehenge.

00:05:56.372 --> 00:05:58.613
So, what about Stonehenge?

00:05:58.673 --> 00:05:59.964
What is its mystery?

00:06:00.024 --> 00:06:01.715
No one really knows.

00:06:01.775 --> 00:06:03.746
Ask Uncle Stephen.

00:06:03.806 --> 00:06:06.278
Tomorrow we can go to see it.

00:06:06.338 --> 00:06:09.730
Suddenly there is a knock at the door.

00:06:09.790 --> 00:06:13.922
Mum opens it and an old man comes in.

00:06:13.982 --> 00:06:17.715
He has white hair and an angry face.

00:06:17.774 --> 00:06:22.170
My name's Carter, he says, in an angry voice.

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:24.354
I look after this cottage.

00:06:24.414 --> 00:06:26.175
Is everything okay?

00:06:26.235 --> 00:06:28.687
There is wood for the fire in the garden.

00:06:28.747 --> 00:06:31.189
There are streets and pillows upstairs.

00:06:31.249 --> 00:06:33.271
If you have a problem, tell me.

00:06:33.291 --> 00:06:36.264
Have you got any problems?

00:06:36.324 --> 00:06:38.616
Now mum remembers.

00:06:38.676 --> 00:06:42.008
Yes, Mr. Carter is the caretaker.

00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:45.441
He looks after the cottage when no one is staying in it.

00:06:45.501 --> 00:06:47.613
Thank you, Mr. Carter.

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:51.576
It's very kind of you, but we have no problems.

00:06:51.636 --> 00:06:56.690
Mr. Carter wants a problem to solve, so he is not very happy.

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:58.482
He goes to the door.

00:06:58.542 --> 00:07:02.595
Then he stops suddenly, turns around and looks at them.

00:07:02.655 --> 00:07:05.778
Mrs. Black is coming, he says.

00:07:05.838 --> 00:07:08.359
Mrs. Black is coming soon.

00:07:08.419 --> 00:07:10.240
Be careful.

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:13.482
He opens the door and goes out.

00:07:13.542 --> 00:07:14.914
What?

00:07:14.974 --> 00:07:16.095
asks Mum.

00:07:16.155 --> 00:07:17.886
Who is Mrs. Black?

00:07:17.946 --> 00:07:19.194
asks Max.

00:07:19.254 --> 00:07:22.064
And why be careful?

00:07:22.124 --> 00:07:23.725
Is she dangerous?

00:07:23.745 --> 00:07:25.646
Pasks Auntie Barbara.

00:07:25.706 --> 00:07:28.649
Probably a witch in Stonehenge.

00:07:28.709 --> 00:07:29.850
Says Laura.

00:07:29.910 --> 00:07:32.562
Everyone laughs.

00:07:32.622 --> 00:07:36.986
Don't talk about things you don't understand.

00:07:37.046 --> 00:07:38.877
Says Uncle Stephen.

00:07:38.937 --> 00:07:42.030
There is another knock at the door.

00:07:42.090 --> 00:07:44.392
They all stop.

00:07:44.452 --> 00:07:47.084
There is silence in the room.

00:07:47.144 --> 00:07:49.488
Max opens the door.

00:07:49.548 --> 00:07:51.602
No one speaks.

00:07:51.662 --> 00:07:53.934
Hello, everyone!

00:07:53.994 --> 00:07:55.694
says a happy voice.

00:07:55.754 --> 00:07:58.055
A woman comes into the cottage.

00:07:58.115 --> 00:08:01.936
She is quite old, fat, but she is pretty.

00:08:01.996 --> 00:08:06.989
She has blue eyes, silver earrings, and a big pink face.

00:08:07.048 --> 00:08:08.709
Hello.

00:08:08.769 --> 00:08:11.210
My name is Mrs. Black.

00:08:11.270 --> 00:08:13.981
Mrs. Black is a housekeeper.

00:08:14.041 --> 00:08:16.588
She helps with the cooking and cleaning.

00:08:16.648 --> 00:08:21.144
When a family comes for a holiday in the cottage, she helps them.

00:08:21.204 --> 00:08:25.576
She lives in a different cottage in the village with her son.

00:08:25.636 --> 00:08:30.577
Mrs. Black is very nice, and they start to relax.

00:08:30.637 --> 00:08:37.339
Later they eat a big dinner, and then say goodbye to their new friend, the housekeeper.

00:08:37.399 --> 00:08:41.520
They are very tired, and soon everyone is sleeping.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:44.983
Everyone but Uncle Stephen.

00:08:45.043 --> 00:08:53.272
He can't sleep because he is thinking about the book he is studying.

00:08:53.332 --> 00:09:19.266
In the morning, Laura and Max decide to explore the small village of Stone Cross.

00:09:19.286 --> 00:09:19.566
Bye!

00:09:19.626 --> 00:09:21.037
Have a nice time.

00:09:21.097 --> 00:09:23.548
Come home for lunch at one o'clock.

00:09:23.608 --> 00:09:25.460
Says their mother.

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:33.913
In the square there is a post office, a bakers, a green roses, a news agent and some other small shops.

00:09:33.973 --> 00:09:36.805
Let's buy something to drink in this news agent.

00:09:36.865 --> 00:09:37.855
Says Max.

00:09:37.915 --> 00:09:39.506
It's very hot.

00:09:39.566 --> 00:09:42.181
A woman is working in the shop.

00:09:42.241 --> 00:09:48.300
They say, good morning, and smile at the woman, but she does not smile at them.

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:51.652
She looks at the twins with cold eyes.

00:09:51.712 --> 00:09:54.634
You two aren't from Stone Cross.

00:09:54.694 --> 00:09:56.296
What do you want?

00:09:56.356 --> 00:09:58.988
The woman is not very friendly.

00:09:59.048 --> 00:10:01.110
Two cans of coke, please.

00:10:01.170 --> 00:10:03.972
Says Max, £1.60.

00:10:04.032 --> 00:10:08.336
She gives them two cans of coke, and they give her the money.

00:10:08.396 --> 00:10:12.021
The woman's cold eyes do not change.

00:10:12.081 --> 00:10:15.245
Taurus don't usually come to Stone Cross.

00:10:15.305 --> 00:10:16.346
She says.

00:10:16.406 --> 00:10:19.028
Her voice is cold too.

00:10:19.088 --> 00:10:21.490
It's not a good idea.

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:23.101
Remember that.

00:10:23.161 --> 00:10:24.172
Uh, yes.

00:10:24.232 --> 00:10:24.992
Okay.

00:10:25.052 --> 00:10:25.853
Thank you.

00:10:25.913 --> 00:10:27.034
Uh, goodbye.

00:10:27.094 --> 00:10:28.224
Says Laura.

00:10:28.284 --> 00:10:31.026
They run out of the shop very quickly.

00:10:31.086 --> 00:10:33.839
In the square, the sun is shining.

00:10:33.898 --> 00:10:35.550
Everything is normal again.

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:37.352
Wow!

00:10:37.412 --> 00:10:39.863
There are some strange people in this village.

00:10:39.923 --> 00:10:41.620
Says Max.

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:46.586
They walk along another street, and suddenly a man appears.

00:10:46.646 --> 00:10:48.576
He is not very old.

00:10:48.636 --> 00:10:53.178
He is wearing a dark suit and a tie with a strange design on it.

00:10:53.238 --> 00:10:54.888
The twins stop.

00:10:54.948 --> 00:10:56.419
The man smiles.

00:10:56.479 --> 00:10:59.419
He says, Hello, hello!

00:10:59.479 --> 00:11:02.430
Two explorers in Stone Cross.

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:03.791
Are you on holiday?

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:05.281
Are you having a nice time?

00:11:05.341 --> 00:11:06.891
Yes, yes, thank you.

00:11:06.951 --> 00:11:08.132
Replies, Laura.

00:11:08.192 --> 00:11:10.072
My name's Martin Knight.

00:11:10.132 --> 00:11:11.414
What are your names?

00:11:11.474 --> 00:11:13.255
Max and Laura Morrell.

00:11:13.315 --> 00:11:14.706
They say together.

00:11:14.766 --> 00:11:18.548
Sometimes twins understand what the other is thinking.

00:11:18.608 --> 00:11:21.490
Sometimes they speak together.

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:23.382
Morrell.

00:11:23.442 --> 00:11:26.874
Is your father the famous historian Stephen Morrell?

00:11:26.934 --> 00:11:27.654
No.

00:11:27.714 --> 00:11:28.815
He's our uncle.

00:11:28.875 --> 00:11:29.966
Not our father.

00:11:30.026 --> 00:11:32.338
He's on holiday with us in Stone Cross.

00:11:32.398 --> 00:11:33.758
Do you know him?

00:11:33.818 --> 00:11:36.928
The man doesn't answer Max's question.

00:11:36.988 --> 00:11:40.217
I see Stephen Morel is here in Stone Cross.

00:11:40.277 --> 00:11:41.557
Very interesting.

00:11:41.617 --> 00:11:45.908
And tell me, what is he studying at the moment?

00:11:45.968 --> 00:11:49.309
Oh, a really old book about mysteries and secrets.

00:11:49.369 --> 00:11:51.429
Sorry, Mr Knight, but it's very late.

00:11:51.489 --> 00:11:53.140
We must go home and have lunch.

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:54.750
Laura stops him.

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:55.770
Come on, Max.

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:56.630
It's time to go.

00:11:56.690 --> 00:11:59.551
Can we meet tomorrow, says Martin Knight?

00:11:59.611 --> 00:12:02.342
You can tell me about your uncle's old book.

00:12:02.402 --> 00:12:03.082
OK.

00:12:03.142 --> 00:12:04.048
Says Max.

00:12:04.108 --> 00:12:05.376
Come on Max!

00:12:05.436 --> 00:12:08.968
Says Laura, and the twins go back along the road.

00:12:09.028 --> 00:12:11.919
Sorry Max, but I don't like that man.

00:12:11.979 --> 00:12:13.329
Explains Laura.

00:12:13.389 --> 00:12:16.400
He wants to know about Uncle Stephen and his books.

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:18.932
But Uncle Stephen is very famous.

00:12:18.992 --> 00:12:20.974
Lots of people want to know about him.

00:12:21.034 --> 00:12:21.634
I know.

00:12:21.695 --> 00:12:23.176
But this man is different.

00:12:23.236 --> 00:12:24.727
I can't explain why.

00:12:24.787 --> 00:12:27.279
Not everyone is strange in Stone Cross.

00:12:27.339 --> 00:12:28.820
Think of Mrs Black.

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:30.862
She's a nice normal woman.

00:12:30.922 --> 00:12:32.443
Yes, you're right.

00:12:32.503 --> 00:12:33.204
Sorry.

00:12:33.264 --> 00:12:34.835
But now it's quarter to one.

00:12:34.895 --> 00:12:38.588
And we must go home.

00:12:38.648 --> 00:12:43.163
Listening activity.

00:12:43.223 --> 00:12:44.836
Good morning.

00:12:44.896 --> 00:12:45.867
Morning?

00:12:45.927 --> 00:12:47.808
Can I have some stamps, please?

00:12:47.868 --> 00:12:49.770
And some postcards too, please?

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:50.671
Yes.

00:12:50.730 --> 00:12:51.752
How many?

00:12:51.812 --> 00:12:57.646
Well, one postcard for Grandmother, one for Uncle Stephen and Auntie Barbara.

00:12:57.706 --> 00:13:01.640
No, Max, Uncle Stephen and Auntie Barbara on holiday with us.

00:13:01.700 --> 00:13:02.700
Oh, yes.

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:08.485
So, one postcard for Grandmother, one for James and one for Amanda.

00:13:08.545 --> 00:13:11.517
So, you want three postcards?

00:13:11.577 --> 00:13:12.367
Yes.

00:13:12.427 --> 00:13:14.219
And three stamps please.

00:13:14.278 --> 00:13:17.060
The postcards cost 20PH.

00:13:17.120 --> 00:13:19.722
The stamps cost 22P.

00:13:19.782 --> 00:13:21.403
I'm not very good at maths.

00:13:21.463 --> 00:13:23.594
Laura, how much is it?

00:13:23.654 --> 00:13:27.406
Three postcards are 60pents and three stamps are 66pents.

00:13:27.446 --> 00:13:28.217
That's £1.26.

00:13:28.277 --> 00:13:29.227
That's right.

00:13:29.287 --> 00:13:30.358
£1.26 please.

00:13:30.418 --> 00:13:31.729
Here you are, £1.50.

00:13:31.789 --> 00:13:34.893
Bye.

00:13:34.953 --> 00:13:38.407
Thank you.

00:13:38.467 --> 00:13:39.178
Goodbye.

00:13:39.198 --> 00:13:44.730
Hey, don't forget your change.

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:50.362
Listen to how we say these prices.

00:13:50.422 --> 00:13:53.353
30 pence.

00:13:53.413 --> 00:13:54.853
55 pence.

00:13:54.913 --> 00:13:56.874
One pound.

00:13:56.934 --> 00:13:59.284
Two pounds 50.

00:13:59.344 --> 00:14:01.896
Four pounds 15.

00:14:01.956 --> 00:14:04.026
Five pounds.

00:14:04.086 --> 00:14:06.277
Six pounds 30.

00:14:06.337 --> 00:15:08.798
£7.99 £8.82 £12 £20 £45 £70 £1.60 £2 £3 £50 £4.99 £5.25 £11.70 £14.40 Chapter 5 of Visit to Stonehenge When the twins get home, everyone is waiting for them.

00:15:08.858 --> 00:15:11.439
Mrs. Black is there too.

00:15:11.499 --> 00:15:14.681
What do you think of our little village?

00:15:14.741 --> 00:15:15.831
She asks.

00:15:15.891 --> 00:15:19.533
The village is lovely, but some of the people are strange.

00:15:19.593 --> 00:15:21.144
replies Laura.

00:15:21.204 --> 00:15:23.395
Mrs. Black laughs.

00:15:23.455 --> 00:15:25.996
I know, I know.

00:15:26.056 --> 00:15:28.397
Don't worry about the people.

00:15:28.457 --> 00:15:30.948
They don't see many tourists.

00:15:31.008 --> 00:15:34.514
Not many people come to Stone Cross.

00:15:34.574 --> 00:15:38.629
Are you ready to go to Stonehenge this afternoon?"

00:15:38.689 --> 00:15:40.580
asks Auntie Barbara.

00:15:40.640 --> 00:15:43.332
Mrs. Beck says.

00:15:43.392 --> 00:15:47.334
Ah, you're going to Stonehenge.

00:15:47.394 --> 00:15:49.766
It's nothing special.

00:15:49.826 --> 00:15:52.118
A circle of old stones.

00:15:52.178 --> 00:15:53.668
That's all.

00:15:53.728 --> 00:15:57.461
Stonehenge is near the village of Stone Cross.

00:15:57.521 --> 00:16:01.264
They take the cars, and in twenty minutes they are there.

00:16:01.324 --> 00:16:03.632
Laura suddenly shouts.

00:16:03.692 --> 00:16:06.600
Look, there it is, there it is.

00:16:06.660 --> 00:16:12.274
And down in the valley they see Mrs Black's circle of old stones.

00:16:12.334 --> 00:16:16.486
Each spectacular, says Uncle Stephen.

00:16:16.546 --> 00:16:18.698
It's incredible.

00:16:18.758 --> 00:16:19.848
Says Mum.

00:16:19.908 --> 00:16:22.110
It's magnificent.

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:23.710
Says Auntie Barbara.

00:16:23.770 --> 00:16:25.022
Wow.

00:16:25.082 --> 00:16:26.162
Says Laura.

00:16:26.222 --> 00:16:27.833
It's not very big.

00:16:27.893 --> 00:16:29.024
Says Max.

00:16:29.084 --> 00:16:30.635
Shut up Max.

00:16:30.695 --> 00:16:32.248
Says everyone.

00:16:32.308 --> 00:16:34.601
Andrew, what do you think?

00:16:34.661 --> 00:16:36.873
Do you like Stonehenge?

00:16:36.932 --> 00:16:37.903
Andrew?

00:16:37.963 --> 00:16:39.674
Dad doesn't answer.

00:16:39.734 --> 00:16:42.256
He is sleeping in the car.

00:16:42.316 --> 00:16:44.567
Andrew, wake up now.

00:16:44.627 --> 00:16:47.758
This time, mum is very angry.

00:16:47.818 --> 00:16:50.720
Around the stones there is a fence.

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:55.453
People can't touch them, but they can go very near and take photographs.

00:16:55.513 --> 00:16:57.514
Let's get an audio guide.

00:16:57.574 --> 00:16:58.696
Suggests mum.

00:16:58.756 --> 00:17:03.120
You listen and it tells you the story of Stone Hange.

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:09.566
Everyone gets an audio guide and they start to walk around the enormous stone circle.

00:17:09.627 --> 00:17:15.501
Uncle Stephen walks in the opposite direction and looks at his old book of mysteries.

00:17:15.562 --> 00:17:19.625
He reads something and then looks at the stones.

00:17:19.686 --> 00:17:22.468
Then he walks away.

00:17:22.527 --> 00:17:26.612
He looks at the hills and the trees near the stones.

00:17:26.671 --> 00:17:31.534
Hmm, three hills around the stones.

00:17:31.594 --> 00:17:34.865
Yes, it is a type of triangle.

00:17:34.925 --> 00:17:36.536
He says to himself.

00:17:36.596 --> 00:17:39.578
Then he looks at the stones again.

00:17:39.638 --> 00:17:42.418
Uncle Stephen is thinking.

00:17:42.478 --> 00:17:46.430
Half an hour later, the others return.

00:17:46.490 --> 00:17:49.542
Stonehenge is fantastic.

00:17:49.602 --> 00:17:50.582
They say.

00:17:50.642 --> 00:17:53.093
But Uncle Stephen is not listening.

00:17:53.153 --> 00:17:55.300
He's reading his book again.

00:17:55.360 --> 00:17:58.698
and looking at the stones and the hills around them.

00:17:58.758 --> 00:18:01.079
Time for something to drink.

00:18:01.139 --> 00:18:02.160
Says Mum.

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:06.182
They all walk to the small cafe near the tourist shop.

00:18:06.242 --> 00:18:07.973
Come on Steven.

00:18:08.034 --> 00:18:09.664
Are you coming with us?

00:18:09.724 --> 00:18:16.964
Finally Uncle Steven puts his book in his bag and follows the others.

00:18:17.024 --> 00:18:21.162
Stonehenge.

00:18:21.222 --> 00:18:26.896
Stonehenge is a very old monument in the south of England.

00:18:26.956 --> 00:18:30.148
We don't know exactly what it is.

00:18:30.208 --> 00:18:31.869
Is it a temple?

00:18:31.929 --> 00:18:35.492
Is it an astronomical observatory?

00:18:35.552 --> 00:18:40.134
Is it from the times of Merlin and King Arthur?

00:18:40.194 --> 00:18:43.126
Stonehenge Factphile.

00:18:43.186 --> 00:18:44.837
Where?

00:18:44.898 --> 00:18:49.544
It is near Salisbury in the south of England.

00:18:49.605 --> 00:18:51.789
When?

00:18:51.849 --> 00:18:58.141
No one knows exactly, but there are three construction periods.

00:18:58.161 --> 00:18:58.851
1.

00:18:58.911 --> 00:19:06.323
In 3000 BC, there is a circular ditch with a diameter of around 100 meters.

00:19:06.383 --> 00:19:06.443
2.

00:19:06.463 --> 00:19:11.474
In 2500 BC, there is the original monument.

00:19:11.534 --> 00:19:16.384
It is made of wood.

00:19:16.444 --> 00:19:21.044
3.

00:19:21.104 --> 00:19:30.618
Between 2500 and 1500 BC, people build the Stone Monument.

00:19:30.678 --> 00:19:33.299
Who?

00:19:33.359 --> 00:19:36.180
There are lots of interesting theories.

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:47.418
Druids, people from Atlantis, Merlin the Magician, aliens, probably primitive British people are the architects.

00:19:47.478 --> 00:19:50.130
Why?

00:19:50.190 --> 00:19:54.304
No one knows, but here are some ideas.

00:19:54.364 --> 00:19:58.847
Perhaps people use Stonehenge to study the sky.

00:19:58.908 --> 00:20:04.382
They want to see the changes in the sun, the moon and the stars.

00:20:04.442 --> 00:20:10.798
With this information, they can understand the seasons and the weather.

00:20:10.858 --> 00:20:19.628
Perhaps Stonehenge is an enormous calendar, an observatory or a computer.

00:20:19.688 --> 00:20:29.224
Perhaps it is a magic temple to an ancient god or the tomb of an important king.

00:20:29.284 --> 00:20:32.166
How?

00:20:32.226 --> 00:20:35.097
This is a mystery too.

00:20:35.158 --> 00:20:40.852
The stones are very big and they are very heavy.

00:20:40.912 --> 00:20:44.134
Some stones are blue stones.

00:20:44.194 --> 00:20:51.168
from the Procelli Mountains in South Wales, 385 kilometers away.

00:20:51.228 --> 00:20:58.920
No one knows how the people moved them.

00:20:58.981 --> 00:21:09.752
Chapter 6.

00:21:09.812 --> 00:21:19.214
The family finally gets back to the cottage.

00:21:19.274 --> 00:21:23.488
Everyone is very happy, but they are also tired.

00:21:23.548 --> 00:21:28.082
The sun is shining and everything seems in perfect order.

00:21:28.143 --> 00:21:31.506
They park the cars and go to the cottage.

00:21:31.566 --> 00:21:34.248
That's strange, says Dad.

00:21:34.308 --> 00:21:36.200
I can't move the key.

00:21:36.260 --> 00:21:37.952
I can't open the door.

00:21:38.012 --> 00:21:39.734
Let's try the other door.

00:21:39.794 --> 00:21:41.029
Mum says.

00:21:41.089 --> 00:21:44.885
They walk to the small door at the back of the cottage.

00:21:44.945 --> 00:21:47.077
Suddenly everyone stops.

00:21:47.136 --> 00:21:48.908
The door is open.

00:21:48.968 --> 00:21:50.288
Impossible!

00:21:50.348 --> 00:21:51.339
Says Laura.

00:21:51.399 --> 00:21:53.740
Only Mrs. Black has got a key.

00:21:53.800 --> 00:21:56.942
None and Auntie Barbara scream.

00:21:57.002 --> 00:21:58.473
Faves!

00:21:58.533 --> 00:21:59.714
They say.

00:21:59.774 --> 00:22:02.625
Inside the cottage there is chaos.

00:22:02.686 --> 00:22:07.658
The cupboards are empty, the drawers are open, and things are on the floor.

00:22:07.718 --> 00:22:09.009
Our money!

00:22:09.069 --> 00:22:10.325
Says Dad.

00:22:10.385 --> 00:22:13.701
My jewellery, says Mum.

00:22:13.761 --> 00:22:17.032
Uncle Stephen says, What's missing?

00:22:17.092 --> 00:22:18.963
We must phone the police.

00:22:19.023 --> 00:22:22.874
They look in all the rooms, but nothing is missing.

00:22:22.934 --> 00:22:25.576
Look, our money is here.

00:22:25.636 --> 00:22:29.127
The thief doesn't want money, says Dad, happily.

00:22:29.187 --> 00:22:32.618
And look, my jewellery is here.

00:22:32.638 --> 00:22:37.030
He doesn't want my diamond ring, says Mum.

00:22:37.090 --> 00:22:40.821
So why, what is interesting for a thief here?

00:22:40.881 --> 00:22:42.642
Ask Max.

00:22:42.702 --> 00:22:46.594
Uncle Stephen's face is very serious.

00:22:46.654 --> 00:22:49.896
I think I know the answer to that question.

00:22:49.956 --> 00:22:56.960
This is what the thief wants, he says, and takes the book of mysteries from his bag.

00:22:57.020 --> 00:22:59.862
That old book, but why?

00:22:59.922 --> 00:23:01.093
Ask Max.

00:23:01.153 --> 00:23:04.816
I am studying the mystery of Stonehenge.

00:23:04.876 --> 00:23:10.450
Some people think that it is an ancient computer, Uncle Stephen explains.

00:23:10.510 --> 00:23:13.992
I don't understand, says Laura.

00:23:14.052 --> 00:23:19.464
Ancient people understand lots of things that we don't understand now.

00:23:19.524 --> 00:23:25.307
Things about the stars, about energy, mathematics and communication.

00:23:25.367 --> 00:23:29.819
We think that Stonehenge is an enormous computer.

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:35.441
It connects information to other ancient computers around the world.

00:23:35.501 --> 00:23:36.811
Like the pyramids.

00:23:36.871 --> 00:23:38.772
Says Laura excitedly.

00:23:38.832 --> 00:23:40.042
Exactly.

00:23:40.102 --> 00:23:45.263
Perhaps these computers communicate with spacemen too.

00:23:45.323 --> 00:23:46.143
Wow.

00:23:46.203 --> 00:23:47.523
Says Max.

00:23:47.583 --> 00:23:50.244
Uncle Stephen continues.

00:23:50.304 --> 00:23:54.394
My old book of mysteries has a secret code.

00:23:54.454 --> 00:23:57.577
But there is a symbol I don't understand.

00:23:57.638 --> 00:24:03.022
I want to understand the symbol, because I want to understand Stonehenge.

00:24:03.082 --> 00:24:08.915
This computer can be very dangerous, because bad people can use the information.

00:24:08.975 --> 00:24:11.856
We must protect the book, do you understand?

00:24:11.916 --> 00:24:14.578
Yes, they all reply.

00:24:14.638 --> 00:24:17.109
Now, let's tidy the house.

00:24:17.169 --> 00:24:20.921
Everyone must keep their eyes and ears open.

00:24:20.981 --> 00:24:24.022
Yes, they all reply.

00:24:24.082 --> 00:24:27.243
The twins are tidying the house.

00:24:27.304 --> 00:24:32.837
Suddenly Laura stops and says, Max, look, what do you think this is?

00:24:32.898 --> 00:24:36.220
She gives her brother a small silver object.

00:24:36.280 --> 00:24:40.934
It is round with a triangle and a strange cross in the middle.

00:24:40.994 --> 00:24:43.096
It's got a pin in the back.

00:24:43.156 --> 00:24:44.317
It's a brooch.

00:24:44.377 --> 00:24:46.789
Yes, perhaps it belongs to the thief.

00:24:46.850 --> 00:24:48.832
Let's give it to Uncle Stephen.

00:24:48.892 --> 00:24:53.440
They tell their uncle the story and he looks at the small object.

00:24:53.500 --> 00:24:57.149
He puts it in his desk, and his face is serious.

00:24:57.209 --> 00:24:59.561
He doesn't say anything.

00:24:59.621 --> 00:25:02.794
Max and Laura go into the living room.

00:25:02.854 --> 00:25:05.696
There's something strange about that object, Laura.

00:25:05.756 --> 00:25:06.768
Says Max.

00:25:06.828 --> 00:25:08.539
I know that symbol.

00:25:08.599 --> 00:25:09.280
Yes.

00:25:09.340 --> 00:25:10.270
Says Laura.

00:25:10.330 --> 00:25:11.402
Me too.

00:25:11.462 --> 00:25:18.246
I recognise it, but where from?

00:25:18.306 --> 00:25:30.423
Chapter Seven, a noisy night.

00:25:30.484 --> 00:25:38.348
At seven o'clock Mrs. Black arrives.

00:25:38.408 --> 00:25:42.176
She helps cook the dinner and listens to the story.

00:25:42.236 --> 00:25:44.452
Terrible, she says.

00:25:44.512 --> 00:25:47.923
Every summer there are thieves in Stone Cross.

00:25:47.983 --> 00:25:51.074
They know there are lots of tourists, you see.

00:25:51.134 --> 00:25:53.254
But you say that tourists don't come here.

00:25:53.314 --> 00:25:54.855
Answers, Laura.

00:25:54.915 --> 00:25:59.166
Oh, yes, erm, well, it depends.

00:25:59.226 --> 00:26:01.836
Some summers, there are a lot.

00:26:01.896 --> 00:26:04.287
Some summers, there aren't a lot.

00:26:04.347 --> 00:26:06.878
Suddenly a telephone rings.

00:26:06.938 --> 00:26:09.888
It is Mrs Black's mobile phone.

00:26:09.948 --> 00:26:14.980
Oh, excuse me, she says, and smiles at everyone.

00:26:15.040 --> 00:26:19.142
She goes to the hall and speaks in a soft voice.

00:26:19.202 --> 00:26:20.252
Yes.

00:26:20.312 --> 00:26:21.513
Yes.

00:26:21.573 --> 00:26:22.794
Okay.

00:26:22.854 --> 00:26:23.904
Don't worry.

00:26:23.924 --> 00:26:26.216
Everything's alright.

00:26:26.276 --> 00:26:27.876
I don't know.

00:26:27.936 --> 00:26:29.307
Perhaps tonight.

00:26:29.367 --> 00:26:31.258
Perhaps tomorrow night.

00:26:31.318 --> 00:26:32.628
Okay.

00:26:32.688 --> 00:26:34.039
Bye.

00:26:34.099 --> 00:26:36.829
My son, she explains.

00:26:36.889 --> 00:26:40.830
He's 27 and he doesn't know how to cook.

00:26:40.890 --> 00:26:42.720
Can you believe it?

00:26:42.780 --> 00:26:44.491
Mum laughs.

00:26:44.551 --> 00:26:47.952
I'm sure he prefers your wonderful cooking.

00:26:48.012 --> 00:26:51.994
Later that evening, everyone is playing cards together.

00:26:52.054 --> 00:26:53.385
Mum is winning.

00:26:53.445 --> 00:26:55.155
She always wins.

00:26:55.216 --> 00:27:01.168
Mrs. Black says, Who wants a nice cup of hot chocolate?

00:27:01.228 --> 00:27:05.539
During the evening and at night, it is cold in the house.

00:27:05.600 --> 00:27:08.400
They say, yes, please, Mrs. Black.

00:27:08.461 --> 00:27:11.542
But Laura says, no, thank you.

00:27:11.603 --> 00:27:13.704
The housekeeper seems offended.

00:27:13.764 --> 00:27:14.794
Why not?

00:27:14.854 --> 00:27:16.165
She asks angrily.

00:27:16.225 --> 00:27:18.537
Hot chocolate helps you sleep.

00:27:18.597 --> 00:27:20.878
I can sleep with no problems, thank you.

00:27:20.938 --> 00:27:22.620
Replies Laura.

00:27:22.680 --> 00:27:28.653
Mrs. Black is not very happy, but goes to the kitchen to make hot chocolate for the others.

00:27:28.713 --> 00:27:32.495
It is creamy, chocolatey, and delicious.

00:27:32.555 --> 00:27:35.785
This is wonderful, Mrs. Black.

00:27:35.845 --> 00:27:38.654
What is the special ingredient?

00:27:38.714 --> 00:27:42.114
Do you have a secret recipe?

00:27:42.174 --> 00:27:46.495
It's my grandmother's secret recipe.

00:27:46.555 --> 00:27:48.796
She says and laughs.

00:27:48.856 --> 00:27:51.686
She says good night and goes home.

00:27:51.746 --> 00:27:56.557
Soon, everyone is very sleepy and goes to bed.

00:27:56.617 --> 00:28:01.498
Only Laura isn't tired.

00:28:01.558 --> 00:28:05.444
It is the middle of the night.

00:28:05.504 --> 00:28:10.144
Outside the sky is full of stars, but there is no moon.

00:28:10.204 --> 00:28:12.205
Everyone is sleeping.

00:28:12.265 --> 00:28:16.108
Mum is dreaming, and Dad is snoring.

00:28:16.168 --> 00:28:19.831
Suddenly, Laura sits up in her bed.

00:28:19.891 --> 00:28:22.233
There is a noise.

00:28:22.293 --> 00:28:25.936
Someone is downstairs.

00:28:25.996 --> 00:28:27.997
She relaxes.

00:28:28.057 --> 00:28:29.968
It is probably her father.

00:28:30.028 --> 00:28:33.710
Me sometimes gets up and sleep walks.

00:28:33.770 --> 00:28:38.312
But no, she can hear her father.

00:28:38.332 --> 00:28:43.005
He is snoring in his bedroom.

00:28:43.065 --> 00:28:47.078
She gets up very quietly.

00:28:47.138 --> 00:28:50.721
Yes, there is someone.

00:28:50.780 --> 00:28:53.392
The noise is in the study.

00:28:53.452 --> 00:28:55.564
She goes downstairs.

00:28:55.624 --> 00:28:58.130
She is very quiet.

00:28:58.191 --> 00:29:02.598
When she is outside the study, she stops and listens.

00:29:02.658 --> 00:29:07.349
She hears the sound of paper.

00:29:07.409 --> 00:29:11.021
I must be brave.

00:29:11.081 --> 00:29:14.662
She says, and pushes the door open quietly.

00:29:14.722 --> 00:29:15.312
Stop!

00:29:15.372 --> 00:29:15.982
Thief!

00:29:16.042 --> 00:29:17.153
She shouts.

00:29:17.213 --> 00:29:20.894
But to her surprise, she sees Mrs. Black.

00:29:20.954 --> 00:29:25.986
She is sitting at Uncle Stephen's desk, reading his notebooks.

00:29:26.046 --> 00:29:26.646
Oh!

00:29:26.666 --> 00:29:28.164
Mrs. Black!

00:29:28.224 --> 00:29:31.082
It's you, says Laura.

00:29:31.142 --> 00:29:33.254
Er, hello Laura.

00:29:33.314 --> 00:29:35.816
I can't find my car keys.

00:29:35.876 --> 00:29:37.528
Perhaps they're here.

00:29:37.548 --> 00:29:40.520
I don't want to disturb everyone.

00:29:40.580 --> 00:29:41.951
Oh, all right.

00:29:42.011 --> 00:29:43.102
Says Laura.

00:29:43.162 --> 00:29:49.546
But then she remembers Mrs. Black hasn't got a car.

00:29:49.606 --> 00:29:53.410
At that moment, Dad and Uncle Stephen arrive.

00:29:53.470 --> 00:29:55.802
They think there is another thief.

00:29:55.862 --> 00:29:58.454
Dad smiles and laughs.

00:29:58.514 --> 00:29:59.746
Phew!

00:29:59.806 --> 00:30:01.658
He's Mrs. Black!

00:30:01.718 --> 00:30:03.479
Hello Mrs. Black!

00:30:03.539 --> 00:30:05.680
You're working late tonight?

00:30:05.740 --> 00:30:08.042
Uncle Stephen doesn't laugh.

00:30:08.102 --> 00:30:11.044
What are you doing in my study, Mrs. Black?

00:30:11.104 --> 00:30:12.736
He asks.

00:30:12.796 --> 00:30:16.538
She tells him the story of the car keys.

00:30:16.598 --> 00:30:22.692
Uncle Stephen replies, Tomorrow we can all look for the keys together.

00:30:22.752 --> 00:30:25.004
Now it's time to sleep.

00:30:25.064 --> 00:30:27.044
Good night, Mrs. Black.

00:30:27.104 --> 00:30:30.945
He opens the door, and the housekeeper goes out.

00:30:31.006 --> 00:30:39.952
She doesn't look at Uncle Stephen when she says, Good night, everyone.

00:30:40.012 --> 00:30:52.299
Chapter 8 Now I remember.

00:30:52.359 --> 00:31:01.954
For two or three days, everything is normal and everyone is happy.

00:31:02.014 --> 00:31:07.128
Mrs. Black says her son has got the car keys, and they aren't lost after all.

00:31:07.188 --> 00:31:12.342
Laura looks at Mrs. Black, but decides not to say anything.

00:31:12.403 --> 00:31:16.296
On Wednesday afternoon, Mum and Dad go walking.

00:31:16.356 --> 00:31:22.793
Dad wants to sleep, but Mum says, No, Andrew, you can't sleep at all.

00:31:22.853 --> 00:31:24.707
Oh, all right.

00:31:24.767 --> 00:31:25.787
He replies.

00:31:25.847 --> 00:31:27.768
But he is not very happy.

00:31:27.828 --> 00:31:29.359
What about you, Stephen?

00:31:29.419 --> 00:31:30.059
Come with us.

00:31:30.119 --> 00:31:31.020
No, thank you.

00:31:31.080 --> 00:31:32.410
I must work.

00:31:32.471 --> 00:31:35.032
Auntie Barbara laughs.

00:31:35.092 --> 00:31:40.424
And says to mum, Sarah, your husband sleeps all the time.

00:31:40.484 --> 00:31:43.236
And my husband works all the time.

00:31:43.296 --> 00:31:44.936
Don't laugh, Barbara.

00:31:44.996 --> 00:31:46.704
Replies, Uncle Stephen.

00:31:46.764 --> 00:31:49.214
My work is very important.

00:31:49.274 --> 00:31:51.226
Everyone laughs.

00:31:51.286 --> 00:31:55.208
Sometimes Uncle Stephen is very funny.

00:31:55.269 --> 00:31:58.121
Today I want to work a lot.

00:31:58.181 --> 00:32:00.513
Please don't disturb me.

00:32:00.573 --> 00:32:03.166
He says and goes to the study.

00:32:03.226 --> 00:32:05.207
Can I come with you to?

00:32:05.267 --> 00:32:06.798
Ask Santa Barbara.

00:32:06.858 --> 00:32:09.220
Of course they reply.

00:32:09.280 --> 00:32:14.680
They all put on their walking boots and say goodbye to the twins.

00:32:14.740 --> 00:32:20.189
Max and Laura decide to explore a different part of the village.

00:32:20.249 --> 00:32:22.790
In the village there is a small hill.

00:32:22.850 --> 00:32:27.352
It is a strange shape and on the top there is a stone cross.

00:32:27.413 --> 00:32:32.395
The village probably has the name stone cross because there is a stone cross on the hill.

00:32:32.455 --> 00:32:33.586
Says Laura.

00:32:33.646 --> 00:32:35.776
Very clever Sherlock.

00:32:35.836 --> 00:32:37.448
Says her brother.

00:32:37.508 --> 00:32:40.409
They look up to the cross on the hill.

00:32:40.469 --> 00:32:43.219
Two people are talking near it.

00:32:43.279 --> 00:32:48.010
The sun is behind them, and the twins can't see very well.

00:32:48.070 --> 00:32:50.252
Who are those two people?

00:32:50.312 --> 00:32:51.843
They ask together.

00:32:51.903 --> 00:32:54.774
Mrs. Black and Martin Knight.

00:32:54.834 --> 00:32:56.316
Let's go and listen.

00:32:56.376 --> 00:32:57.446
Says Max.

00:32:57.506 --> 00:32:58.897
No, Max.

00:32:58.957 --> 00:32:59.768
Says Laura.

00:32:59.828 --> 00:33:00.948
We must listen to it.

00:33:01.008 --> 00:33:02.459
Suddenly she stops.

00:33:02.519 --> 00:33:04.250
Her face is white.

00:33:04.310 --> 00:33:07.172
Max, now I remember.

00:33:07.232 --> 00:33:09.804
Max's face is white too.

00:33:09.864 --> 00:33:12.546
He remembers the same thing.

00:33:12.606 --> 00:33:13.818
I know.

00:33:13.878 --> 00:33:15.120
Me too.

00:33:15.180 --> 00:33:16.471
The symbol.

00:33:16.530 --> 00:33:17.471
Yes.

00:33:17.532 --> 00:33:19.113
I know where it comes from.

00:33:19.173 --> 00:33:19.974
Yes.

00:33:20.034 --> 00:33:21.925
Mrs. Black's earrings.

00:33:21.985 --> 00:33:23.586
It's the same symbol.

00:33:23.646 --> 00:33:24.487
What?

00:33:24.547 --> 00:33:27.219
I remember it from Martin Knight's tie.

00:33:27.279 --> 00:33:28.050
What?

00:33:28.110 --> 00:33:32.724
This means Mrs. Black and Martin Knight know the thief.

00:33:32.784 --> 00:33:35.095
Perhaps one of them is the thief.

00:33:35.155 --> 00:33:39.068
Do you remember Mrs. Black reading Uncle Steven's notebook?

00:33:39.128 --> 00:33:41.785
Do you remember Martin Knight's questions?

00:33:41.845 --> 00:33:43.191
What can we do?

00:33:43.251 --> 00:33:44.422
Come on, Laura.

00:33:44.482 --> 00:33:45.452
Follow me.

00:33:45.512 --> 00:33:46.814
Says Max.

00:33:46.874 --> 00:33:52.428
They start to go up the hill, but Mrs Black and Martin Knight aren't there.

00:33:52.488 --> 00:33:53.939
We're too late.

00:33:53.999 --> 00:33:55.160
Where are they now?

00:33:55.220 --> 00:33:56.110
Says Laura.

00:33:56.170 --> 00:33:57.011
I don't know.

00:33:57.071 --> 00:33:58.072
Answers Max.

00:33:58.132 --> 00:33:58.732
Come on.

00:33:58.792 --> 00:34:01.624
Let's go home and tell Uncle Stephen what we know.

00:34:01.684 --> 00:34:12.973
They start to walk home, but on the hill two dark shadows are watching them from behind the stone cross.

00:34:13.033 --> 00:34:29.579
Famous Detectives The Famous Five by Enid Blyton The Famous Five are a group of child detectives, really four children and a dog.

00:34:29.639 --> 00:34:37.051
Three of the children, Julian, Dick and Anne are brothers and sister.

00:34:37.111 --> 00:34:45.051
During their holidays, they usually go to stay with their aunt, uncle and cousin Georgina.

00:34:45.111 --> 00:34:52.362
Georgina prefers the name George and has a dog called Timmy.

00:34:52.423 --> 00:34:58.827
The five always have adventures and solve mysteries.

00:34:58.887 --> 00:35:08.962
Miss Marple by Agatha Christie Another famous detective is an old lady with white hair.

00:35:09.022 --> 00:35:12.304
Her name is Miss Marple.

00:35:12.364 --> 00:35:14.554
She is about 70.

00:35:14.614 --> 00:35:16.814
and she's not married.

00:35:16.874 --> 00:35:22.826
She lives in a very small village in England, like Stone Cross.

00:35:22.886 --> 00:35:35.202
It is a quiet village, but Miss Marple meets lots of people there, a postman, a village policeman, a hairdresser.

00:35:35.262 --> 00:35:40.065
She talks to these people and listens to their stories.

00:35:40.125 --> 00:35:49.023
She discovers lots of information about crime.

00:35:49.083 --> 00:35:54.910
Chapter 9.

00:35:54.971 --> 00:36:03.206
Uncle Stephen understands.

00:36:03.266 --> 00:36:08.650
Uncle Stephen is happy.

00:36:08.710 --> 00:36:11.862
Finally, he can work in peace.

00:36:11.922 --> 00:36:15.585
He makes a cup of tea and goes into his study.

00:36:15.646 --> 00:36:22.794
On his desk, there is the old book of mysteries and the silver broach with the strange symbol.

00:36:22.854 --> 00:36:26.368
He takes the approach in his hand and looks at it.

00:36:26.428 --> 00:36:29.020
He knows it is part of the mystery.

00:36:29.080 --> 00:36:30.700
But how?

00:36:30.760 --> 00:36:34.092
The circle is similar to Stonehenge.

00:36:34.152 --> 00:36:37.643
The triangle is similar to the hills around it.

00:36:37.703 --> 00:36:40.964
But what does the cross mean?

00:36:41.024 --> 00:36:44.066
Uncle Stephen recognizes the symbol.

00:36:44.126 --> 00:36:46.718
But where from?

00:36:46.778 --> 00:36:49.808
He drinks some more tea.

00:36:49.868 --> 00:36:51.486
He thinks.

00:36:51.546 --> 00:36:54.284
He looks out of the window.

00:36:54.344 --> 00:37:02.468
From the window he can see the strange hill in the village and the strange stone cross on the top of it.

00:37:02.528 --> 00:37:05.300
Wait a minute, he thinks.

00:37:05.360 --> 00:37:08.742
The strange stone cross.

00:37:08.802 --> 00:37:10.483
He looks at the brooch.

00:37:10.543 --> 00:37:13.864
Yes, it's the same.

00:37:13.924 --> 00:37:17.807
He quickly turns to a page in his old book of mysteries.

00:37:17.867 --> 00:37:20.071
He reads something and shouts.

00:37:20.131 --> 00:37:22.805
Yes, now I understand.

00:37:22.865 --> 00:37:24.336
Now I understand.

00:37:24.356 --> 00:37:28.728
I must telephone Professor Johnson in London.

00:37:28.788 --> 00:37:31.970
He takes the phone and calls the number.

00:37:32.031 --> 00:37:34.132
Hello, Professor.

00:37:34.192 --> 00:37:36.793
It's Stephen Morrell here.

00:37:36.853 --> 00:37:39.774
Listen, we must meet.

00:37:39.834 --> 00:37:42.446
Can I bring the book to you in London?

00:37:42.506 --> 00:37:44.457
It's not safe here.

00:37:44.517 --> 00:37:47.069
There's a train at five o'clock this evening.

00:37:47.129 --> 00:37:50.063
It gets to London at seven o'clock.

00:37:50.123 --> 00:37:51.526
Yes.

00:37:51.586 --> 00:37:53.317
See you at the station.

00:37:53.377 --> 00:37:54.568
Goodbye.

00:37:54.628 --> 00:37:55.838
And thank you."

00:37:55.898 --> 00:37:59.390
He puts the phone down and picks up his cup of tea.

00:37:59.450 --> 00:38:02.832
I'm sure that tea's cold now.

00:38:02.892 --> 00:38:05.383
Says a cold voice behind him.

00:38:05.443 --> 00:38:10.105
He turns quickly and sees the shadow of Mrs. Black in the door.

00:38:10.165 --> 00:38:11.806
What are you doing here?

00:38:11.866 --> 00:38:13.226
He asks angrily.

00:38:13.286 --> 00:38:14.897
You don't work today.

00:38:14.957 --> 00:38:15.757
What do you want?

00:38:15.818 --> 00:38:19.231
Mrs. Black's earrings shine in the sun.

00:38:19.291 --> 00:38:22.166
You know what I want, Morale.

00:38:22.226 --> 00:38:28.203
She says, give me that book.

00:38:28.263 --> 00:38:36.500
Listening activity.

00:38:36.560 --> 00:38:41.772
Hello, Professor.

00:38:41.792 --> 00:38:43.733
It's Stephen Morrell here.

00:38:43.753 --> 00:38:45.314
Ah, morning, Morrell.

00:38:45.374 --> 00:38:46.114
How are you?

00:38:46.174 --> 00:38:46.915
Not bad.

00:38:46.975 --> 00:38:47.885
Thank you, Professor.

00:38:47.945 --> 00:38:48.685
And you?

00:38:48.745 --> 00:38:49.946
Fine, thanks.

00:38:50.006 --> 00:38:52.147
Listen, we must meet.

00:38:52.207 --> 00:38:54.848
Can I bring the book to you in London?

00:38:54.908 --> 00:38:56.389
Yes, but why?

00:38:56.449 --> 00:38:58.040
It's not safe here.

00:38:58.100 --> 00:38:59.280
I understand.

00:38:59.340 --> 00:39:01.641
What time can you arrive in London?

00:39:01.701 --> 00:39:04.492
There's a train at five o'clock this evening.

00:39:04.552 --> 00:39:06.843
It gets to London at seven o'clock.

00:39:06.903 --> 00:39:09.018
Seven o'clock this evening.

00:39:09.078 --> 00:39:09.854
All right.

00:39:09.914 --> 00:39:11.014
See you at the station.

00:39:11.074 --> 00:39:11.635
Yes.

00:39:11.695 --> 00:39:12.956
See you at the station.

00:39:13.016 --> 00:39:14.127
All right, Morrell.

00:39:14.187 --> 00:39:14.857
Goodbye.

00:39:14.917 --> 00:39:15.598
Goodbye.

00:39:15.658 --> 00:39:20.852
And thank you.

00:39:20.912 --> 00:39:25.966
Chapter 10.

00:39:25.986 --> 00:39:33.140
A Doctor's Visit.

00:39:33.200 --> 00:39:44.255
Max and Laura play near a river for some time, but later go back to the cottage.

00:39:44.315 --> 00:39:46.356
Everything is quiet.

00:39:46.416 --> 00:39:50.318
They don't have a key, so they knock on the door.

00:39:50.378 --> 00:39:52.879
Nobody answers.

00:39:52.939 --> 00:39:55.700
They knock again.

00:39:55.760 --> 00:39:59.342
And Mrs. Black answers the door.

00:39:59.402 --> 00:40:04.684
She is wearing an apron and she has a rolling pin in her hand.

00:40:04.745 --> 00:40:08.529
She says, Hello, children.

00:40:08.589 --> 00:40:12.632
I'm making a delicious chocolate cake for lunch.

00:40:12.692 --> 00:40:16.516
Your Uncle Stephen doesn't feel very well.

00:40:16.576 --> 00:40:20.630
Your parents aren't here, and I want to help.

00:40:20.690 --> 00:40:21.890
What do you mean?

00:40:21.951 --> 00:40:23.612
Uncle Stephen's fine.

00:40:23.672 --> 00:40:24.804
Says Max.

00:40:24.864 --> 00:40:27.396
He has a headache and a temperature.

00:40:27.456 --> 00:40:29.087
Mrs. Black replies.

00:40:29.147 --> 00:40:31.840
He works too hard.

00:40:31.900 --> 00:40:33.648
This is very strange.

00:40:33.708 --> 00:40:35.865
Uncle Stephen is never ill.

00:40:35.925 --> 00:40:39.216
Max and Laura don't believe the housekeeper.

00:40:39.276 --> 00:40:41.276
I once told my uncle.

00:40:41.336 --> 00:40:42.376
Says Laura.

00:40:42.437 --> 00:40:43.427
Me too.

00:40:43.487 --> 00:40:44.897
Says Max.

00:40:44.957 --> 00:40:47.867
Mrs. Black is a big woman.

00:40:47.927 --> 00:40:51.788
She stands in the door and the twins can't pass.

00:40:51.848 --> 00:40:54.439
It's not a good idea.

00:40:54.499 --> 00:40:55.559
She tells them.

00:40:55.619 --> 00:40:57.839
Your uncle is upstairs.

00:40:57.899 --> 00:40:59.509
He's resting.

00:40:59.569 --> 00:41:02.060
I want to see my uncle now.

00:41:02.120 --> 00:41:03.358
Repeats Laura.

00:41:03.418 --> 00:41:05.356
You can't see him!

00:41:05.416 --> 00:41:07.467
There is a doctor with him now!

00:41:07.527 --> 00:41:10.048
Mrs. Black shouts.

00:41:10.109 --> 00:41:14.040
Laura pushes the woman and she falls to the floor.

00:41:14.100 --> 00:41:16.271
Max runs past her, too.

00:41:16.331 --> 00:41:19.322
They go to the study, but their uncle is not there.

00:41:19.382 --> 00:41:21.194
They run upstairs.

00:41:21.254 --> 00:41:24.565
Uncle Stephen, are you all right?

00:41:24.625 --> 00:41:27.676
Shouts Laura, but there is no answer.

00:41:27.736 --> 00:41:30.528
Max opens the bedroom door.

00:41:30.588 --> 00:41:33.300
Uncle Stephen is lying on the bed.

00:41:33.360 --> 00:41:37.544
He cannot move his arms or legs because there is a rope around them.

00:41:37.604 --> 00:41:42.268
There is a big bump on his head and his eyes are closed.

00:41:42.328 --> 00:41:43.598
If he did.

00:41:43.658 --> 00:41:45.970
Asked Laura in a frightened voice.

00:41:46.030 --> 00:41:47.821
No, he's sleeping.

00:41:47.881 --> 00:41:49.062
Max replies.

00:41:49.122 --> 00:41:50.673
Look, he's breathing.

00:41:50.733 --> 00:41:52.684
Yes, he's sleeping.

00:41:52.744 --> 00:41:54.816
Says a familiar voice.

00:41:54.876 --> 00:41:57.958
They look up and see a man in the room.

00:41:58.018 --> 00:41:59.859
Marty Knight.

00:41:59.919 --> 00:42:01.662
They say together.

00:42:01.723 --> 00:42:03.826
Oh yes, he laughs.

00:42:03.886 --> 00:42:05.866
Your uncle is sleeping.

00:42:05.926 --> 00:42:11.218
Now we can take his book and discover the secret of the stones.

00:42:11.278 --> 00:42:18.031
Now no one can stop us, especially two stupid children.

00:42:18.091 --> 00:42:22.072
At that moment Mrs. Black arrives.

00:42:22.132 --> 00:42:24.344
I see you know my son.

00:42:24.404 --> 00:42:25.554
She says.

00:42:25.614 --> 00:42:28.427
She is holding the rolling pin.

00:42:28.487 --> 00:42:32.752
Suddenly, Max understands what she wants to do.

00:42:32.812 --> 00:42:34.453
Quick, Laura!

00:42:34.513 --> 00:42:36.685
He pushes his sister to the floor.

00:42:36.745 --> 00:42:39.287
The rolling pin misses Laura's head.

00:42:39.347 --> 00:42:40.658
Max jumps up.

00:42:40.718 --> 00:42:43.350
He tries to take the rolling pin for Mrs Black.

00:42:43.410 --> 00:42:45.482
Laura gets up and starts to run away.

00:42:45.502 --> 00:42:50.446
Martin Knight tries to stop her, but she is very fast.

00:42:50.506 --> 00:42:54.968
Suddenly, outside, they hear the sound of a siren.

00:42:55.029 --> 00:42:57.290
It is a police car.

00:42:57.350 --> 00:42:58.720
Quick!

00:42:58.781 --> 00:42:59.701
The police!

00:42:59.761 --> 00:43:01.102
Shouts Martin.

00:43:01.162 --> 00:43:04.045
He and Mrs Black run.

00:43:04.105 --> 00:43:07.528
When they arrive at the door, there are two policemen waiting for them.

00:43:07.588 --> 00:43:11.952
They put handcuffs on the two criminals and push them into the police van.

00:43:12.012 --> 00:43:15.734
Laura telephones for an ambulance for Uncle Stephen.

00:43:15.794 --> 00:43:18.728
Max speaks to the policeman.

00:43:18.788 --> 00:43:20.048
Thank you.

00:43:20.108 --> 00:43:20.999
He says.

00:43:21.059 --> 00:43:24.762
But I don't understand why...

00:43:24.822 --> 00:43:26.179
He stops.

00:43:26.240 --> 00:43:30.227
Under a tree in the garden, he sees an old man.

00:43:30.247 --> 00:43:32.648
Mr. Carter.

00:43:32.708 --> 00:43:35.708
Mr. Carter comes and talks to Max.

00:43:35.768 --> 00:43:40.760
Remember, boy, you must tell me your problems, he says.

00:43:40.820 --> 00:43:42.670
I know these people.

00:43:42.730 --> 00:43:44.541
I know this place.

00:43:44.601 --> 00:43:47.052
I know when there's a problem.

00:43:47.112 --> 00:43:47.962
Thank you.

00:43:48.022 --> 00:43:49.072
Says Max.

00:43:49.132 --> 00:43:52.153
You're welcome, the old man smiles.

00:43:52.213 --> 00:44:00.342
Now, how about a nice cup of tea?

00:44:00.402 --> 00:44:05.999
Chapter 11.

00:44:06.059 --> 00:44:14.351
The secret of the stones.

00:44:14.412 --> 00:44:20.473
The next day, everyone is at the hospital.

00:44:20.533 --> 00:44:22.694
Uncle Stephen is in bed.

00:44:22.754 --> 00:44:26.014
The doctor says that there is only one problem.

00:44:26.074 --> 00:44:29.465
The big bump on Uncle Stephen's head.

00:44:29.525 --> 00:44:32.652
Uncle Stephen opens his eyes.

00:44:32.712 --> 00:44:34.909
Hello, Barbara.

00:44:34.970 --> 00:44:36.320
What day is it?

00:44:36.380 --> 00:44:38.200
It's Thursday, darling.

00:44:38.260 --> 00:44:39.461
Oh, hello, Andrew.

00:44:39.521 --> 00:44:41.532
Hello, everyone.

00:44:41.592 --> 00:44:43.992
What are you doing here?

00:44:44.052 --> 00:44:46.993
Don't you have school today, children?

00:44:47.053 --> 00:44:48.373
It's the summer holiday.

00:44:48.433 --> 00:44:49.944
Laura replies.

00:44:50.004 --> 00:44:52.674
We're in Stone Cross, remember?

00:44:52.734 --> 00:44:53.865
Says Max.

00:44:53.925 --> 00:44:56.025
Stone Cross?

00:44:56.086 --> 00:44:57.236
Holiday?

00:44:57.256 --> 00:45:00.036
No, I don't remember.

00:45:00.096 --> 00:45:01.942
We're in London.

00:45:02.002 --> 00:45:05.469
I think Uncle Stephen doesn't remember.

00:45:05.530 --> 00:45:10.833
He doesn't remember about the holiday, about Mrs. Black and Martin Knight.

00:45:10.893 --> 00:45:17.547
And most important of all, he doesn't remember about the secret of the stones.

00:45:17.608 --> 00:45:22.260
He remembers the symbol, the brooch, the old book of mysteries.

00:45:22.320 --> 00:45:24.072
They ask him.

00:45:24.132 --> 00:45:29.906
He smiles and says, no, sorry.

00:45:29.966 --> 00:45:32.210
A policeman arrives.

00:45:32.270 --> 00:45:40.464
He tells them that the two criminals, Martin Smith and his mother, Dorothy Smith, are part of a secret organization.

00:45:40.524 --> 00:45:44.917
The name of the organization is the Black Knights, he says.

00:45:44.977 --> 00:45:51.271
They want to find the secret of Stonehenge, and use the secret to become rich and powerful.

00:45:51.331 --> 00:45:55.304
Mr. Morrell is the only person who knows the secret.

00:45:55.364 --> 00:45:59.340
But I don't know the secret, says Uncle Steven.

00:45:59.400 --> 00:46:03.728
I'm sorry everyone, but I can't remember.

00:46:03.788 --> 00:46:07.862
Perhaps it's the best thing, says Auntie Barbara.

00:46:07.922 --> 00:46:12.446
The stones can keep their 5,000 year old secret.

00:46:12.506 --> 00:46:15.780
It's not right to take it from them now.

00:46:15.840 --> 00:46:17.642
Everyone agrees.

00:46:17.702 --> 00:46:21.145
Perhaps we can find another secret next holiday.

00:46:21.205 --> 00:46:23.404
Say Max and Laura together.

00:46:23.464 --> 00:46:27.085
Perhaps next holiday I can stay in London.

00:46:27.145 --> 00:46:28.816
Says Uncle Stephen.

00:46:28.876 --> 00:46:31.988
He rubs the bump on his head.

00:46:32.048 --> 00:46:34.951
Poor Uncle Stephen.

00:46:35.012 --> 00:46:38.103
Everybody laughs.

00:46:38.164 --> 00:46:41.516
No more adventures this summer.

00:46:41.576 --> 00:46:42.638
Says Max.

00:46:42.698 --> 00:46:44.629
But perhaps at Christmas.

00:46:44.689 --> 00:46:46.350
Says Laura.

00:46:46.410 --> 00:46:50.684
Who knows?

00:46:50.744 --> 00:46:55.586
Listening activity.

00:46:55.646 --> 00:46:58.988
Hello, I'm Detective Wood.

00:46:59.048 --> 00:47:01.539
Can I ask you some questions, please?

00:47:01.599 --> 00:47:02.869
Yes, of course.

00:47:02.929 --> 00:47:04.360
Right.

00:47:04.420 --> 00:47:06.820
Just one moment, please.

00:47:06.880 --> 00:47:08.911
Where's my pen?

00:47:08.971 --> 00:47:10.672
Look, it's on the desk.

00:47:10.732 --> 00:47:11.757
Thank you.

00:47:11.818 --> 00:47:14.514
Now, what day is it today?

00:47:14.574 --> 00:47:16.956
It's Thursday, it's half past three.

00:47:17.016 --> 00:47:19.527
Oh yes, and the month is August.

00:47:19.588 --> 00:47:21.569
Okay, let's start.

00:47:21.629 --> 00:47:24.771
What's your name, and where do you come from?

00:47:24.831 --> 00:47:27.632
My name's Laura Morrell, and I come from London.

00:47:27.692 --> 00:47:29.003
How old are you, Laura?

00:47:29.063 --> 00:47:30.844
I'm 13 in October.

00:47:30.904 --> 00:47:33.276
Have you got any brothers or sisters?

00:47:33.336 --> 00:47:35.637
Yes, I've got one brother, Max.

00:47:35.697 --> 00:47:36.898
He's my twin brother.

00:47:36.958 --> 00:47:38.674
And how old is he?

